---
import RelatedLinks from '../components/RelatedLinks.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy | ReadyGearHub" description="ReadyGearHub's privacy policy: what information we collect, how we use it, and your choices.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="fine light">Last updated November 20, 2026</p></div></section>
  <section class="wrap section prose">
    <p>ReadyGearHub is operated by {site.legalName}, {site.addressLocality}, {site.addressRegion}. You can reach us at <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a> or through our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Information you send us.</strong> If you use our contact or listing request forms, we receive what you type, such as your name, email, business name, and message. We use it only to reply and to evaluate listing requests.</li>
      <li><strong>Email list.</strong> If you sign up for our email list, MailerLite (our email provider) collects the address and any name you enter, so we can send the occasional checklists and seasonal reminders you asked for. You can unsubscribe at any time from the link in those emails, or by emailing us.</li>
      <li><strong>Basic technical data.</strong> Our hosting provider (Netlify) may log standard information like IP address, browser type, and pages requested, for security and performance.</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics.</strong> We use Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity to understand how people use the site — for example which pages are popular and which links are clicked. These tools may set cookies or use similar storage on your device, and they collect anonymous usage information such as pages viewed, approximate location, and device type. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a> and <a href="https://www.microsoft.com/privacy/privacystatement">Microsoft's privacy statement</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Advertising measurement.</strong> If you arrive from a Google ad, or complete a signup after clicking one, we use the Google Ads tag (loaded with Google Analytics) to measure whether an ad led to a visit or a signup. That tag may set cookies or use similar storage. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads">Google's advertising privacy information</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Affiliate links and third-party sites</h2>
    <p>When you click a link to a brand or retailer, you leave ReadyGearHub. That site may use cookies to track the referral, including for affiliate commissions. Their privacy policies apply on their sites. If you buy a ReadyGearHub digital product, checkout is handled by Payhip, and Payhip's privacy policy applies to the information you give them to complete the purchase and deliver the download.</p>
    <h2>What we don't do</h2>
    <p>We don't sell your personal information. We don't send marketing emails unless you've asked to receive them.</p>
    <h2>Tools and alerts in your browser</h2>
    <p>Some ReadyGearHub tools — live weather alerts, the outage timer, the kit builder, and Storm Tracker — can save your choices (such as a selected state or county, or an outage start time) in your browser's local storage so they are still there when you return. That information stays on your device; these tools do not send it to ReadyGearHub's servers. If you arrive from a paid ad, the site also stores a short paid-session flag in your browser's session storage so we can hide offers that those advertising programs do not allow us to show on paid visits. The flag is cleared when you close the tab.</p>
    <p>If you click "Use my location" on the alerts page, your browser may share your coordinates with the National Weather Service (<a href="https://api.weather.gov/">api.weather.gov</a>) to look up alerts for that point. Location is requested only after you click the button, and you can refuse the permission prompt.</p>
    <h2>Your choices</h2>

    <p>You can ask us to access or delete information you've sent us by emailing <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>ReadyGearHub is not directed to children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect their information.</p>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy. The date at the top shows when it last changed.</p>
  </section>
  <RelatedLinks links={[
    { href: "/about/", icon: "ℹ️", title: "About ReadyGearHub", text: "How we choose listings and stay independent." },
    { href: "/refund-policy/", icon: "↩️", title: "Refund policy", text: "Final sale for digital downloads, with a refund if a file is broken." },
    { href: "/affiliate-disclosure/", icon: "🏷️", title: "Affiliate disclosure", text: "How affiliate links work on this site." },
    { href: "/contact/", icon: "💬", title: "Contact us", text: "Questions, corrections, or product suggestions." },
    { href: "/updates/", icon: "✉️", title: "Community safety updates", text: "An occasional, quiet email list." },
    { href: "/guides/", icon: "📘", title: "Guides & checklists", text: "Plain-English prep guides for storms, outages, and water." },
    { href: "/gear/", icon: "📚", title: "Gear directory", text: "Hand-picked gear sorted into simple lanes." }
  ]} />
</Base>
